---
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
  The client-side search index. Every post, as plain text.

  `plain_text` is _plugins/search_index.rb rather than `strip_html |
  strip_newlines`: it decodes HTML entities (kramdown escapes a literal `>` to
  `&gt;`) and leaves a space at block boundaries, so `<p>끝</p><p>시작</p>` is two
  words, not one.

  There is no `snippet` field: js/search.js cuts the shown excerpt around the
  match in `content`.

  Every field here is searched: simple-jekyll-search walks each key and matches a
  post when all query words appear in one of them.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
  {% for post in site.posts %}
    {
      "title": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
      "url": "{{ site.baseurl }}{{ post.url }}",
      "date": "{{ post.date | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}",
      "category": {{ post.categories | join: ', ' | jsonify }},
      "tags": {{ post.tags | join: ', ' | replace: '-', ' ' | jsonify }},
      "content": {{ post.content | plain_text | jsonify }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]
